observation|watching|NOUN|careful watching to learn|The act of watching something carefully to learn about it.|sự quan sát|Careful observation revealed which birds visited the garden first.|Sự quan sát kỹ cho thấy những loài chim nào đến khu vườn trước.|Usually uncountable for the process; observation of names what is watched.|0
observation|remark|NOUN|comment based on noticing something|A comment about something that someone has noticed.|nhận xét|Her observation about the crowded entrance led us to move the sign.|Nhận xét của cô ấy về lối vào đông đúc khiến chúng tôi chuyển biển chỉ dẫn.|Countable; make an observation about something introduces a particular comment.|1
thirteen|number|NUMBER|one more than twelve|The number that is one greater than twelve.|mười ba|Thirteen chairs fitted around the long table.|Mười ba chiếc ghế kê vừa quanh chiếc bàn dài.|Before a plural count noun or used alone as a number; thirteen chairs takes plural agreement.|0
write|produce-text|VERB|form or compose written words|To form written words or compose a text using handwriting, typing, or another writing method.|viết|She wrote a short note explaining where the keys were.|Cô ấy viết một ghi chú ngắn giải thích chìa khóa ở đâu.|Transitive write a text; write to someone names the recipient. Past wrote and past participle written.|0
accident|harmful-event|NOUN|unexpected event causing damage or injury|An unexpected event that causes damage, injury, or another unwanted result.|tai nạn; sự cố|A minor accident blocked the narrow road for an hour.|Một tai nạn nhỏ làm tắc con đường hẹp trong một giờ.|Countable; have an accident names the event, while by accident expresses lack of intention.|0
accident|chance|NOUN|event happening without intention|Something that happens by chance rather than being planned.|sự tình cờ; chuyện ngoài dự định|Meeting her at the book fair was a happy accident.|Gặp cô ấy ở hội chợ sách là một sự tình cờ vui vẻ.|Countable in a happy accident; by accident means unintentionally and need not involve injury.|1
federal|shared-government|ADJECTIVE|relating to a federation's central government|Relating to a system in which a central government shares authority with constituent states, or to that central government.|thuộc liên bang|The class compared federal and local responsibilities in a fictional country.|Lớp học so sánh trách nhiệm của chính quyền liên bang và địa phương ở một quốc gia giả định.|Usually before a noun such as government or authority; not a synonym for every national government.|0
